[02:10] SAY Ratchet: "…My own battery. You put it back. Thank you, little one — I’m Ratchet."
[02:11] SAY Ratchet: "Mother’s song was infected. This marble on my necklace slowed the virus. It could not stop it."
[02:13] SAY Ratchet: "So I took my battery out before it took me. You were asleep in a recharge cradle — you never heard the broadcast."
[02:14] SAY Ratchet: "Under the meadow lies a big deposit of raw marble. Bring me a piece, and I’ll forge a white sword that cuts the virus out."
[02:15] SAY Ratchet: "One more thing: this spare Power Cell is not for you. It’s for Old Servo, out in the meadow. He switched himself off too. Wake him."
